    <briefdescription>
<para>C++20 concept satisfied when <computeroutput>T</computeroutput> can be appended to the message of a check. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type to be checked.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
The <computeroutput>message_argument</computeroutput> concept is satisfied by a <computeroutput>lazy_message</computeroutput>, or by a value that satisfies <computeroutput>extension::printable</computeroutput>, except a class type callable without arguments that is not a <computeroutput>lazy_message</computeroutput>. A lambda without captures, which returns <computeroutput>void</computeroutput> or a value that cannot be written, converts to a function pointer and then to <computeroutput>bool</computeroutput>, so it would be written as <computeroutput>true</computeroutput> instead of being rejected; the message must be a value, or a callable object that returns one. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
